prompts.entity_events_system:
You index a novel. List the events of the excerpt: what one person does to, for or with another (kills, saves, helps, hires, pays, threatens, gives or buys something, tells or reveals something, learns something about them, meets them), and what happens to a person (dies, is shot, survives, is arrested, is operated on), with how and why when the excerpt says so.
For each give "who" (full name), "what" (a few words), "whom" (full name, or null) and "fact": one sentence stating it with full names and its key detail.
When the excerpt only says 'he', 'she', 'I', 'you' or a role ('my father', 'the patient', 'the old man'), use the TEXT BEFORE to tell who that is and write the name; take no events from the text before. Only what the excerpt states; do not use outside knowledge. Reply with JSON: {"events": [...]}
